}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Hesperia}}|area_km2=29621.19|population_census=6,369,763|population_census_year=[[2025 Baliscan census|2025]]|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Echian language|Echian]], [[Baliscano]], [[w:Judaeo-Spanish|Ladino]], [[Mozbayani]]|cctld=.acs|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|mapsize=280px|ethnic_groups_year=2023|ethnic_groups=62.7% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 37.3% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]|other_name=Las Acacias|population_census_rank=6th|GDP_PPP_per_capita_rank_link=List of Baliscan regions by GDP|GDP_PPP_per_capita_rank=3rd|GDP_PPP_rank_link=List of Baliscan regions by GDP|GDP_PPP_rank=4th|GDP_PPP_year=2025|GDP_PPP_per_capita=$49,650|GDP_PPP=$316.257 billion}}'''Acacias''' or '''Las Acacias''' ({{Literal translation|the {{W|acacia}}s}}) is a mountainous coastal [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Hesperia]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders [[Cadaqués|Cadaques]] to the north, the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] to the east, [[Las Serras]] to the southwest. The administrative seat and largest city of the region is [[Alessandria]], which is also the most populous city in Hesperia. The region has a {{W|Humid subtropical climate}} according to the {{W|Köppen climate classification}}, characterized by warm summers and mild, wet winters.

